1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,920
This is InventDB Legal.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:08,920
Practice management for law firms, built on InventDB SOAR.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,920
A missed deadline can become a malpractice claim.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,420
A trust account error can become a State Bar complaint.

5
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:18,420
Unbilled time is a fee the firm never collects.

6
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:20,920
InventDB Legal is built around all three.

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,420
Sign in, and the firm's day is on one page:

8
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:31,920
730 open matters, 172 deadlines due in 30 days, $1.27 million in trust.

9
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,920
Deadlines first. Missed deadlines are a common cause of malpractice claims.

10
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:42,420
Each is counted from its rule: here, Rule 8.121(a), ten days from the notice of appeal.

11
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:45,420
Limitation dates are tracked on every matter.

12
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:50,420
Hearings, depositions and mediations share one court calendar.

13
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:54,920
The docket report lists everything due in the next 30 days.

14
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,920
A workflow emails each attorney their critical deadlines.

15
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:03,920
Then client money: trust errors are a common cause of State Bar discipline.

16
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:09,920
Every deposit, transfer and disbursement is entered on the client's own ledger.

17
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:15,920
The monthly reconciliation shows no client ledger ever went below zero.

18
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:23,920
Settlements show the gross, the fee, costs, each lien and the net to the client.

19
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,420
Billing: every hour counts.

20
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:32,420
Time carries UTBMS phase, task and activity codes, the coding insurers ask for.

21
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:36,920
Unbilled work: $300,640 at standard rates.

22
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:41,920
Invoices show write-downs, trust applied and the balance due.

23
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:46,920
Receivables are aged, so the oldest money gets chased first.

24
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,920
Ask the practice a question in plain English.

25
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:55,420
Business Litigation holds the most unbilled work: $125,158.50.

26
00:01:55,500 --> 00:02:00,920
Every answer shows its SQL. Analyze only reads.

27
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:02,920
New business.

28
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:08,420
The statute of limitations is worked out the day an enquiry arrives.

29
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:13,920
A conflict check runs, and a person clears it before anyone gives advice.

30
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:19,420
Every matter is one file: 1,300 of them in the demo firm.

31
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:24,420
Court, judge, case number, fee terms, the team, marked Privileged.

32
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:27,920
Its papers are filed with it.

33
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,920
New matters can be described in plain English.

34
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:37,920
Each person sees only the parts of the firm their work needs.

35
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:41,920
It works on a phone at the courthouse,

36
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,920
in light or dark.

37
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:50,420
Built on InventDB SOAR: one database, its sign-in, and row-level security on every request.

38
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:53,920
Covered by 1,300+ backend and 600+ end-to-end tests.

39
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,920
InventDB Legal: the docket, client trust and billing in one place.

